-`phase-16` prompt for the checklist.
+`.github/workflows/build.yml` builds a release APK and a Windows release bundle
+on every push and **opens each one to assert what is inside it**: a
+`classes.dex`, an `libpixelsmith_core.so` for every ABI that ships a
+`libflutter.so`, and — for Windows — `pixelsmith_core.dll` sitting *next to* the
+EXE. An APK with no native library opens fine and throws on the first resize, and
+no build log says so.
+
+The signing workflow is `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which cuts a **draft**
+release from a tag, attaches the artefacts, their SHA-256 sums and the SBOM. It is
+signing-optional by design: with the four Actions secrets in
+[docs/RELEASE.md §4](https://github.com/authorss81/pixelsmith/blob/main/docs/RELEASE.md)
+it signs with a Play upload key; without them it produces a release-mode APK
+signed with the standard Android debug key and says so in the release body. The
+release runbook, including what a release is and is not, is
+[docs/RELEASE.md](https://github.com/authorss81/pixelsmith/blob/main/docs/RELEASE.md).
 
